We have identified and resolved the issues impacting the application launch. Below is a summary of the findings and fixes implemented:


Managed Identity Configuration

We identified that the incorrect managed identity was being used.
The application was configured with the wrong identity (user-assigned/system-assigned mismatch).
We updated the configuration with the correct managed identity, which resolved the issue.



Application Shortcut Configuration

Under Shortcut → Properties → Advanced, the "Run as Administrator" option was enabled.
This caused the application to prompt for admin credentials and subsequently fail.
We unchecked the "Run as Administrator" option, which resolved the issue.



Auto Login Failure

We worked with Brian High to investigate the auto-login issue.
He added the required account to the authorized user list and included it in the AppSupport group.
After these changes, the auto-login functionality started working successfully.



Following the above fixes, we have successfully validated the application launch and functionality. The application is now launching successfully without any issues.
As the issue has been resolved, we are closing this thread.
Thank you to everyone involved in troubleshooting and resolving the problem.
